;; Deliberate defects, each with the test namespace that must notice it.
;;
;; Run with `bb mutate`. Every entry is applied to the source, the named tests
;; are run, and the source is put back. A mutation that no test notices is
;; reported as MISSED and fails the task.
;;
;; This exists because a test that has never been seen to fail has not been
;; shown to test anything. Two real examples, both found by running this:
;;
;;   - packaging_test searched the build script for the string "jdk.localedata"
;;     and passed with the module removed, because the name also appears in the
;;     script's own error message.
;;   - the parser that replaced it matched the words "--add-modules replaces"
;;     out of a comment and returned the module list #{"replaces"}, on which
;;     every assertion was vacuous.
;;
;; Neither announced itself. Both were ordinary-looking green tests.
;;
;; Each :find must appear exactly once and must be the real defect, not a
;; syntactic accident: breaking a function so it throws proves only that the
;; tests call it. The mutations below each reintroduce a fault this project has
;; actually shipped or nearly shipped.

[{:label     "restate does nothing — the R80 bug: 65,000 in a German window"
